# Line endings are load-bearing here, not cosmetic.
#
# The C# analyzers are enforced in-build and warnings fail the build, so a file that arrives
# with LF endings fails the gate — a `sed -i` pass over a .cs file has done exactly that more
# than once. The shell scripts have the opposite requirement: CRLF makes them unrunnable.
# Declaring both stops it depending on whose machine, editor or worktree wrote the file.
# `agent-guard.js` denies `sed -i` on C# for the same reason.

* text=auto

*.cs text eol=crlf
*.csproj text eol=crlf
*.sln text eol=crlf

*.sh text eol=lf
*.js text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
